# What stays OUT of the ROOT knowledge graph (`graphify-out/`).
#
# Syntax is `.gitignore` syntax, and graphify reads this file AFTER
# `.gitignore` — so it can only ever exclude MORE, never re-include something
# `.gitignore` already dropped. Adding a line here is safe in exactly one
# direction: the graph gets narrower, never wider.
#
# Read `knowledge/README.md` before adding an entry — it carries the
# rationale for every rule below and the federated (root + apps/cms) model
# this file is one half of.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# apps/cms/** — the subtree already owns a Graphify graph. Do not duplicate it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `apps/cms` is `ahliweb/awcms` embedded whole via `git subtree` (AGENTS.md,
# "The subtree embed"). It carries its OWN `.graphifyignore`,
# `graphify-out/graph.json` (tracked, ~19 MB, 12700+ nodes), and its own gate
# (`bun run graph:artifacts:check` inside `apps/cms`). Extracting it again
# from the root would:
#
#   - build a second, competing graph authority for the same code, which
#     disagrees with the first the moment either one is rebuilt alone;
#   - roughly double the size of every rebuild this workspace commits to
#     history, for content that is already committed once, correctly, inside
#     the subtree;
#   - give every node two `source_file` identities (root-relative and
#     `apps/cms`-relative), which is exactly the "duplicate extraction
#     producing contradictory node identities" risk issue #11 names.
#
# The federated view over BOTH graphs is `knowledge:graph:combine`
# (`tools/knowledge-graph-combine.mjs`), which merges this root graph with
# `apps/cms/graphify-out/graph.json` via `graphify merge-graphs` into a
# gitignored, on-demand location — never by re-extracting `apps/cms` here.
#
# `bun run knowledge:check` enforces this line stays in force AND that the
# tracked root `graph.json` holds no node whose `source_file` starts with
# `apps/cms/` — a rebuild run from the wrong directory, or with this file
# missing, re-admits what is excluded here, and that is precisely what the
# gate exists to catch.
apps/cms/

