# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Translation mirrors (`*.id.md`) — the source is indexed, not both halves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ADR-0097 (via `ahliweb/awcms`'s own convention, adopted here — see
# AGENTS.md's "Language") makes English at the bare path the source and
# Indonesian at `<name>.id.md` a mirror that records the hash of the English
# it was translated from. A mirror therefore RESTATES its source word for
# word, in another language: indexing both puts every concept into the graph
# twice, for a second copy that contributes no sentence the first did not.
#
# `apps/cms/.graphifyignore` measured this exact rule there (256 mirrors,
# landing after its last graph build, would have doubled a wave of content
# with nothing new to say) and excluded it for the same reason. This root
# corpus is far smaller today, but the shape of the defect does not depend on
# corpus size: a pair of documents with identical content clusters into two
# adjacent, near-indistinguishable communities, and community naming — human
# or hub-based — cannot tell them apart.
#
# This root graph's DEFAULT build is `--code-only` (see `knowledge/README.md`
# — semantic/doc extraction is opt-in, never automatic), so this rule has no
# effect on today's tracked `graph.json`. It is written now, ahead of that
# need, so the first person who opts into semantic extraction here inherits
# the same guard `apps/cms` already needed instead of rediscovering it.
*.id.md

